This is the template to collect proposals for technical initiatives that can accelerate ELISA's mission and help WGs and SIGs deliver tangible, publicly visible results. We are particularly interested in efforts that are constrained by limited contributor capacity, missing expertise, or lack of funding. Selected initiatives should provide clear benefits to the ELISA ecosystem and create opportunities for broader community participation.

1. What's the name of the technical initiative?  
 


2. Who will be the lead(s) for the initiative? Please provide the full name and email address for the lead(s).

3. Please briefly describe the initiative. 

4. Please describe how this initiative supports ELISA’s objectives and how it helps existing WGs or SIGs achieve concrete outcomes.

5. What tangible deliverables do you expect within the next 6–12 months? (e.g reference implementation, tooling, documentation, best-practice guide, demonstrator, training material, assessment framework, etc.)

6. What is currently preventing progress? (Select all that apply)  
- [ ] Lack of contributors  
- [ ] Lack of technical expertise  
- [ ] Lack of funding  
- [ ] Lack of coordination across projects  
- [ ] Missing infrastructure  
- [ ] Other, please specify

7. Is this initiative already being worked on by another open source project or community? If yes, please provide details.

8. If funding is required, please briefly describe the expected funding needs.(This is considered as indication instead of binding. An initial estimate is sufficient.)

9. If this initiative is not pursued by ELISA, what opportunities, technical capabilities, or community benefits would be lost or delayed?

